.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt SVCD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm svcd
.Nd RavenBSD PID 1 service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the name of the PID 1 process implemented by
.Xr init 8 .
It reads the service manifests, starts services in dependency order, serves the
.Dq svc:
control scheme and supervises restarts.
.Pp
A
.Dq STOP
request terminates the service process with the authorized termination primitive, waits for the
terminal state and releases the service's scheme name before reporting success.
.Dq RESTART
stops the old process before starting the replacement.
.Pp
When
.Nm
exits, the process-wide exit terminates its server and worker threads; helper threads blocked in
.Dv PROC_WAIT
do not keep the process or console alive.
See
.Xr init 8
for the manifest format, readiness modes and test settings.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcctl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
